WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.200
Could this ribbon really be nine centimetres long?

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:04.240
Look closely!

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:06.395
It starts at two, not zero.

00:00:06.395 --> 00:00:11.888
Today, let's learn to measure the distance between the marks, rather than just reading the last number.

00:00:11.888 --> 00:00:14.888
Before we calculate, what length do you predict?

00:00:14.888 --> 00:00:18.850
Follow the spaces with your finger, and keep your answer in mind.

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:20.850
Now trace from two to nine.

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:23.610
Each equal space is one centimetre.

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:26.228
We count seven spaces altogether!

00:00:26.228 --> 00:00:28.508
Nine minus two equals seven.

00:00:28.508 --> 00:00:31.388
So, the ribbon is seven centimetres long.

00:00:31.388 --> 00:00:33.067
Did your prediction match?

00:00:33.067 --> 00:00:34.267
Great thinking!

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:36.747
Moving the ruler cannot stretch the ribbon.

00:00:36.747 --> 00:00:40.403
Check the start, count the intervals, then explain your answer.
